  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery, particularly the maximum loss, and assigns greater importance to losses than to gains. In this case, both lotteries involve only losses or zero outcomes (no gains). Lottery A has a maximum loss of -6000 Euros with a 0.1% probability, while Lottery B has a maximum loss of -3000 Euros with a 0.2% probability. The more favorable maximum loss is -3000 Euros (Lottery B), as it is smaller in magnitude than -6000 Euros. Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B due to its less severe maximum loss.",
